{"type": "message", "id": "6f12f84d", "parentId": "3abdae7c", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T12:48:52.755Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_j04v0jci8bgqy16uzvvnviko", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"arXiv cs paper chart model accuracy vs time figure 8\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 3000,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bf5ddd994348744d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nImpact of Accuracy on Model Interpretations Brian Liu Cornell University\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bf5ddd994348744d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.09903\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8c7fe15916994087\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>between [0.8, 1.0].</strong> For each accuracy bucket, we record the interpre- tation stability and trueness for each feature explanation method fit · on each dataset. We then compute the mean metric of each accuracy ... Figure 4: Average Metrics vs.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8c7fe15916994087\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e3dd590798ef9401\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEvaluating time series forecasting models\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e3dd590798ef9401\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1905.11744\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d50fdf7067569c0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nregarding its forecasting accuracy. In this work we evaluate models according to root · mean squared error (RMSE). This metric is traditionally used for measuring the dif- ferences between the estimated values and actual values. ... These analyses are reported in Figures 10–12.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4d50fdf7067569c0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f16f505a17daa16\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTime Series Information Visualization – A Review of Approaches and Tools\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f16f505a17daa16\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.14920\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"546401d5638fcc27\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDepending on the context, the charts share similar structures (e.g., size and type of metaphor), and side-by-side positioning can enhance the estimation of temporal information, minimizing the overloads generated by a single and complex visualization, which may be cognitively tiring [136]. On the other hand, the accuracy of information estimation may decrease, as displaying multiple and simultaneous charts requires each of them to be constructed in smaller portions of space, which can lead to occlusions and reduced details [115]. Figure 3 shows examples of the shared- and split-space visualization systems.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"546401d5638fcc27\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"September 23, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2bf04a13e3614770\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nArtificial Intelligence\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2bf04a13e3614770\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/list/cs.AI/new\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d44dcff4a055306\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTitle: Reasoning Graphs: Deterministic Agent Accuracy through Evidence-Centric Chain-of-Thought Feedback ... Comments: 15 pages including appendix, 2 figures, 3 algorithms, framework paper with evaluation protocol · Subjects: Artificial Intelligen